From: redfin port <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] redfin: orientation events carry the sensor-time child CoreMotion needs

CoreMotion's CLOrientationNotifier::onIohidEvent (in backboardd for BKOrientationManager, and in
locationd) reads the sample time with sensorTimeFromHidChildEvent(): the first child of the
orientation event must be a vendor-defined event, usage page 0xff15 usage 2, with 8 data bytes (a
uint64 sensor time). notifyAOO then drops every sample whose time is not newer than the last one.
Our 0971 orientation events have no children, so the time reads as 0 and every rotation is dropped
("Skipping stale orientation (4 @ 0)" in backboardd's CoreMotion log, r59a 2026-10-29), so
BKOrientationManager never sees a device orientation and the UI never rotates.

Attach that child with the event's mach timestamp (monotonic, so always newer).
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp |  9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
@@ -1241,8 +1241,17 @@
 		int64_t o = sweet_f2q(s->v[0], 1, 1, 0);
 		event = IOHIDEvent::orientationEvent(ts, kIOHIDOrientationTypeCMUsage);
 		if (event) {
 			event->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldOrientationDeviceOrientationUsage,
 			    (SInt32)(gSweetKnobs.orientbase + o));
+			/* 1031: CoreMotion (sensorTimeFromHidChildEvent) wants child 0 = vendor event
+			 * {0xff15, 2} with an 8-byte sensor time; without it every sample is "stale". */
+			uint64_t st = ts;
+			IOHIDEvent *child = IOHIDEvent::vendorDefinedEvent(ts, 0xff15, 2, 0, (UInt8 *)&st,
+			    (UInt32)sizeof(st));
+			if (child) {
+				event->appendChild(child);      /* the children array retains it */
+				child->release();
+			}
 		}
 		snprintf(line, sizeof(line), "UIDeviceOrientation %lld (usage %lld)", o, gSweetKnobs.orientbase + o);
 		break;
